{"/api/discogs/artist/13031/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"13031","image":"https://i.discogs.com/pF_XnX5LhWFwYmP6i-NhOjQzaJ9WvMGOydrA3fvl7vU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:401/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEzMDMx/LTEyMjgzMDY3NDEu/anBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/L5XfQ26q3wL_b_jW5hUsVcQEqP1abpOSrup4REfVFps/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEzMDMx/LTEyMjgzMDY3NDEu/anBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Marcus Intalex was a pseudonym used by [a498175] (born Burnley, Lancashire, 14 July 1971, - died 28 May 2017, Manchester, England) a British Drum 'n' Bass DJ and producer. He was the owner of [l=Soul:r], [l=Revolve:r] and [l=Birdie (2)]. He used to promote the Guidance night in Manchester, as well as hosting shows on Kiss FM (Manchester) and Galaxy FM. He also worked on the jungle counter in Eastern Bloc records.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:13031","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":15790,"name":"Kosh"},{"id":498175,"name":"Marcus Kaye"},{"id":2492078,"name":"Trevino"},{"id":6848254,"name":"Art Vandelay (4)"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Intalex","M. Intalex","Marcus Da Intalex","Marcus Intallex","Marcus Intelex","Marcus Interlex","Mark Da Intallex"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/13031-Marcus-Intalex","type":"artist","urls":["http://twitter.com/marcusintalex","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Intalex"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/15556/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"15556","image":"https://i.discogs.com/wcluyapN6WFnxAXgJtEl_-R7SPKf4KOfB2ufbiJSOTg/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:419/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE1NTU2/LTEzOTQ1NjE5MDkt/NTUzMy5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/il4wMtykX2HTdqQGsyM5ysHoiB00_A_mfJ4GBr8PCRY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE1NTU2/LTEzOTQ1NjE5MDkt/NTUzMy5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Uk garage/hip hop collective from Battersea, South London. Rose through their shows on pirate radio station Delight FM, occupying most of the Sunday schedule which became known as 'So Solid Sundays'. The emphasis on MCs during the period where the darker side of UK garage side was developing would be an early influence towards what would develop later into grime.\r\n\r\nSo Solid's first single \"Oh No\" would arrive in 2000, followed by breaking into the UK top 40 with \"21 Seconds\" (UK no.1), \"They Don't Know\" (no. 3), and \"Haters\" (no. 8). These would all appear on their debut album \"They Don't Know\" released in October 2001, reaching no. 6 in the UK album charts. \r\n\r\nTheir follow up album \"2nd Verse\" would follow in September 2003. Various members have also had solo success and produced for others, and So Solid were still touring into 2013.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:15556","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":20995,"name":"PDS"},{"active":true,"id":81966,"name":"Dan Da Man"},{"active":true,"id":83561,"name":"Lisa Maffia"},{"active":true,"id":93013,"name":"AC Burrell"},{"active":true,"id":109764,"name":"Morgan (4)"},{"active":true,"id":201276,"name":"Thug Angel"},{"active":true,"id":201278,"name":"Tiger S"},{"active":true,"id":214716,"name":"Kowdean"},{"active":true,"id":655800,"name":"DJ Mex (2)"},{"active":true,"id":724485,"name":"Karl Daniel"},{"active":true,"id":851473,"name":"Marvin Dawkins"},{"active":true,"id":985781,"name":"Jason Moore (4)"},{"active":true,"id":1203630,"name":"Darren Weir"},{"active":true,"id":1315512,"name":"Ashley Walters"},{"active":true,"id":1576888,"name":"Mark Oseitutu"},{"active":true,"id":1576889,"name":"Alex Rivers"},{"active":true,"id":1615858,"name":"Shane Neil"},{"active":true,"id":1667627,"name":"G. Phillips (2)"},{"active":true,"id":1906857,"name":"Dwayne Vincent"},{"active":true,"id":2203335,"name":"J. Williams (9)"},{"active":true,"id":3163374,"name":"Pierre Neil"},{"active":true,"id":3264632,"name":"M. J. Harvey"},{"active":true,"id":80